=== CO3 Q6: TLS 1.2 vs TLS 1.3 vs QUIC HANDSHAKE TIMING ===
  TCP + TLS 1.2       : 3 RTT = 300 ms | 1 RTT TCP + 2 RTT TLS 1.2
  TCP + TLS 1.3       : 2 RTT = 200 ms | 1 RTT TCP + 1 RTT TLS 1.3
  QUIC (1st visit)    : 1 RTT = 100 ms | Combined transport + TLS 1.3 in 1 RTT
  QUIC (0-RTT resume) : 0 RTT =   0 ms | Early data sent in initial packet (0 RTT)

1. 0-RTT Replay Risk:
   - An attacker on the network can capture and replay the initial 0-RTT ClientHello + early data.
   - NEVER send non-idempotent requests (e.g., money transfer, password change, POST payments) in 0-RTT;
     only safe idempotent GET requests may use 0-RTT.

2. Connection Migration (Wi-Fi -> 5G):
   - TCP breaks when IP changes because sockets are bound to the 4-tuple (srcIP, srcPort, dstIP, dstPort).
   - QUIC identifies sessions via a cryptographic Connection ID (CID), surviving IP/port changes seamlessly.

3. Corporate Firewall UDP/443 Blocking:
   - Firewalls blocking outbound UDP/443 cause QUIC to time out -> banking app must race/fallback via
     Happy Eyeballs (RFC 8305 / RFC 9114) to TCP + TLS 1.3 over port 443.

--- Live TLS Handshake Inspection (Python ssl + curl HTTP/3 check) ---
  www.google.com    : version=TLSv1.3 | cipher=TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 | tcp=135.5ms | tls=48.5ms | CN=www.google.com
  www.cloudflare.com: version=TLSv1.3 | cipher=TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 | tcp=98.2ms | tls=31.0ms | CN=www.cloudflare.com
  HTTP/3 Alt-Svc (https://www.google.com): Alt-Svc: h3=":443"; ma=2592000,h3-29=":443"; ma=2592000
  HTTP/3 Alt-Svc (https://www.cloudflare.com): alt-svc: h3=":443"; ma=86400

--- Engineering Decision: Should the Banking App Use QUIC? ---
  YES: Cuts cold setup from 300 ms (TLS 1.2) / 200 ms (TLS 1.3) to 100 ms (QUIC) and 0 ms on resume,
       survives Wi-Fi<->5G roaming mid-session, with automatic Happy Eyeballs TCP+TLS 1.3 fallback.

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: Wi-Fi -> 5G Handoff Mid-Transfer (30 s transfer, 100 ms RTT) ---
  - TCP + TLS 1.3 : Connection resets; must redo DNS/TCP (100 ms) + TLS 1.3 (100 ms) + HTTP resume + slow start (>= 300-500 ms lost).
  - QUIC          : Connection ID migrates path in 0 handshake RTTs (0 ms lost to handshake; only path validation ping).
